@@@!atrep

@@@/
Litogramma — strict canonical literary markup, defined as a
dialektos of atrep (Atreptos Platform Specification v0.10).

This is the working dialect definition (.dia). The canonical
litogramma.lektos is produced by kanonizo once tooling exists.

Provisional items are marked with references to
atrep-feedback.md (F1..F9): parts of this dialect depend on
spec v0.10 gaps tracked there. Tentative symbol allocations
are marked TENTATIVE (see HISTORY.md section 2).
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Top matter
======================================================================
/@@@

@@::koine
@@::at-prosa
@@::at-poesia
@@::at-drama
@@::at-aphanes
@@::at-epimerismos

@@@/
======================================================================
Document structure
Headings are enclosing para-simmeres: the section's content is
the grammata. Numbered variants carry an explicit taxis; the
old trailing-period convention is retired.
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Inline formatting
======================================================================
/@@@

@=== math
@$ grammata $@
@"inline math (LaTeX-style content)"@
===@

@=== math-block
@$$[(taxis)]
grammata
$$@
@"display math; taxis present iff the equation is numbered"@
===@

@@@/
Verbatim: no dialect sims. Litogramma inherits the core
enlexis forms (inline and block verbatim), with code-language
tags expressed as genoses on the enlexis episim.
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Lists
The old single-line collapse exception is retired: items and
definitions are uniformly para-simmeres.
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Verse
PROVISIONAL: depends on F1 (stichoi declarability — the
stichos/strophe keywords below are proposed, not yet in spec
v0.10) and F2 (stichoi whitespace preservation in kanonizo).
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Drama
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Notes
Each note family is a single para-simmere definition; the callout
is a deixis (@^(onym) and kin) - the core pointing-reference form
adopted with spec v0.10.1 from feedback F5, so callout and body
share the symbol by construction, with no second definition.
Inline note forms are atramento sugar, not canonical. Canonical
placement (all definitions at document end: footnotes, then
chapter endnotes, then endnotes) is a validation constraint, not
a transform. Deixes and their targets' onyms survive litosis with
fresh autonumbering (F4 resolved for callouts).
======================================================================
/@@@

@=== manuscript-note
@^!
grammata
!^@
@"manuscript note definition; onymized on the episim"@
@""
Critical-edition apparatus or editorial-process annotation;
not part of the Text itself.
""@
===@

@@@/
======================================================================
Asides
The insertion point is a deixis (@|(onym)); the former
aside-point sim is retired with F5's resolution.
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Quotations
======================================================================
/@@@

@@@/
======================================================================
Figures and tables
======================================================================
/@@@

@=== figure
@<[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
<@
@"figure; grammata is an enmedia inclusion plus the caption"@
@""
Bracket matching disabled (episim is the same left angle).
Media files are bundled and hashed by kanonizo; the old res/
directory and ampersand-onym linkage are retired.
""@
===@

@=== table
@+[(taxis)] [lemma]
stichos
+@ [hypograph]
@"table (PROVISIONAL: F1; row/cell model TENTATIVE)"@
@""
Stichoi grammata: one row per stichos, cells separated by
pipes, a dash-run stichos separating a header row. The
hypograph is the caption. Multi-paragraph cells are not
supported.
""@
===@

@@@/
======================================================================
Semantic containers
Named containers carry hash-significant semantics and are
therefore sims, not genoses. Ad-hoc kinds use the generic
container with a genos.
======================================================================
/@@@

@=== container
@_[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
_@
@"generic semantic container; kind given by a genos"@
===@

@=== theorema
@_=[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
=_@
@"theorem container"@
===@

@=== propositio
@_-[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
-_@
@"proposition container"@
===@

@=== lemma
@_:[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
:_@
@"lemma container (the mathematical statement kind)"@
===@

@=== demonstratio
@_/[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
/_@
@"proof container"@
===@

@@@/
======================================================================
References and index
Callout-style references are monosims (F4 applies). The old
curly-brace and delimiter-family pointer syntax is retired.
======================================================================
/@@@

@=== heading-ref
@>>(onym)
@"reference to the closest enclosing heading of an onym"@
@""
An explicit level prefix restricts the heading level, colon-
separated inside the parameter.
""@
===@

@=== page-ref
@>>>(onym)
@"page-number reference"@
===@

@=== line-ref
@>>>>(onym)
@"line-number reference (critical editions)"@
===@

@=== cite
@>[(key)
@"bibliographic citation (TENTATIVE symbol; F7 for keys)"@
@""
The parameter is a citation key resolved against bibliogramma
entries (the atrep-based, BibTeX-isomorphic reference
extension defined beside this dialektos): an entry whose lemma
equals the key, embedded in the document as a bibliogramma
englossis block or carried alongside it. Exports pair through
associated exos - the LaTeX exo routes embedded bibliogramma
content into the companion .bib.
""@
===@

@=== standards-ref
@>: grammata :>@
@"standards reference, rendered as-is (ISO, GOST, case law)"@
@""
A citation-like reference so universally recognized in context
that it needs no bibliography entry.
""@
===@

@@@/
Deferred sims (pending upstream feedback, see atrep-feedback.md):
ref-with-text and component extraction (F9), hidden-href link
plus URL-definition block (F9).
/@@@
